module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_deploy_that_observes_its_own_service_cannot_repair_it" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: CurrentRungUnstatedAfterClimb },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the modeled deploy route (fleet-converge dashboard_deploy, gunbc.live_deploy) derives its plan by observing the running service, and a running service whose /healthz answers non-2xx makes that observation REFUSE -- so the only sanctioned route to replace a broken release requires the release not to be broken. The route can install a release that breaks the service and then cannot install any release at all, rollback included.",

    "HARM, 2026-09-29: after dashboard_deploy run 36584004074 left gunbc-roadmap answering HTTP 500 (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode a_serve_contract_widened_for_one_handler_refuses_every_other), the rollback dashboard_deploy run 36593744640 at 361db9017b refused before acting: 'the deployment plan could not be derived from the host: service-process: refused -- could not observe the host: the process is active but /healthz refused'. Recovery needed an out-of-band operator step (stopping gunbc-roadmap.service by hand at 16:25) before the modeled route could proceed.",

    "WHY IT IS A CLASS AND NOT AN INCIDENT: the observation conflates two facts -- 'the host cannot be observed' (a transport or principal failure, where refusing is right) and 'the service is observed and unhealthy' (a reading, where the plan's job is to replace it). Treating the second as the first makes health a precondition of repair. DESIGN section 5 wants the unhealthy reading to be a typed observed state the plan can act on, not an absorbing refusal of the whole transaction.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable (the failure is loud and located, and an operator can break the deadlock by hand). CEILING: 3 -- the service-process observation can type an unhealthy-but-observed process as its own arm and the plan can derive a replace-release step from it. NEXT TRIGGER: the live_deploy service-process observation distinguishes observed-unhealthy from unobservable, and a dashboard_deploy over an observed-unhealthy process at a different expected_revision plans the replacement instead of refusing; evidence is a fixture with a 500-answering /healthz that plans, beside the existing refusal for an unreachable host.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-11, srv1 workspace bring-up findings ledger F11 (broken deploy blocks its own redeploy; related F01, F46, F52), ledger v3 numbering, operator review of source pinned to main at acc218340ed6e24a9ad06c550a5494307d0320bb (a source review that did not rerun srv1; F11 repeated on the srv1 lab that day). ProcessRunningRelease carrying a revision, or ProcessNotRunning carrying an active flag: an active service whose /healthz fails becomes MemberUnobservable, which decide_member refuses (gunbc.live_deploy.member_observe, member_identity). There is still no representation of an observable, owned, active service with a broken health or release endpoint, so repair requires the damaged service to cooperate. An arbitrary 403 must not become absent. Domain assessment owns the decision; a generic satisfaction Boolean is insufficient (D14). Roadmap leaf cc-observation-distinctions.",

    "OCCURRENCE, 2026-10-15 22:4xZ (THIRD; DEPLOY-UNHEALTHY-1). The operator-approved main-tip prod apply at 87cf694fb90 refused at plan with no mutation: 'live_deploy: the deployment plan could not be derived from the host: service-process: refused -- could not observe the host: the process is active but /healthz refused: http client GET failed within the 240 s probe deadline derived from the serve wall limit; tailnet door cutover refused with no route effect: the cutover journal could not be read, so an interrupted cutover cannot be ruled out: read refused: reply undecodable: HTTP 502'. Prod had been crash-looping since 2026-10-14 21:00Z from a half-applied deploy -- new binary over the old tree -- so systemd reported ActiveState=active (a unit in a restart flurry is active) while /healthz refused, and the observation folded that pair into 'could not observe the host', the SAME arm as an unreachable host. The recovery the row had been climbing was not available: repairing prod required prod to be healthy. Recovery went out of band again -- the operator decided to run tree-sync's own ExecStart by hand. THIS OCCURRENCE IS WHAT MET THE NEXT TRIGGER: it showed both facets at once. (a) The service-process facet, now closed: the probe's ANSWER is typed distinctly from its ABSENCE -- extdeps.http.client GetWithinWithStatus asks for a status line without curl's --fail (a 5xx is an answer, a refused connection is not), gunbc.live_deploy.readiness healthz_effective_read_from_status_get keeps HealthzProbeRefused for a transport failure and yields HealthzAnsweredUnhealthy only when the server-error class answered AND the body identifies no release, member_observe renders that as ProcessObservedUnhealthy inside MemberObserved rather than MemberUnobservable, and decide_member (D14 -- the domain assessment, not a Boolean) plans replace-release over it when the installed revision (read from the tree member's own observation, installed_release_position) differs from the candidate. Guards kept: an arbitrary 403 keeps its body verdict (never absent, never a replacement trigger); a reply that names a release is read as that release whatever its status; a transport failure still refuses; an unreadable installed revision refuses rather than guessing a difference. (b) The door-cutover facet, deliberately NOT weakened: the journal read went through the fabric-storage service this same deploy repairs (HTTP 502), so the journal store's health read as a precondition of repairing the journal store. The interrupted-cutover refusal itself stands verbatim -- refusing because an interrupted cutover cannot be ruled out is sound safety, and it was reproduced unchanged (test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_deploy_witness a_502_journal_read_still_refuses_the_cutover_with_no_route_effect, the_apply_gate_still_refuses_an_unreadable_journal_in_the_ledgers_words, CONTROL/green on main). The cyclic precondition was a STARVATION, not an ordering bug: live_deploy_tailnet_door_cutover_gate already runs downstream of the plan fold, and the admitted mutate steps restart the fabric-storage unit unconditionally (gunbc.live_deploy.emit fabric_storage_admitted_mutate_steps), so the moment facet (a) stopped refusing the plan, the store is repaired before its journal is read. No reordering was built and no deploy may proceed with the door route unverified; the fork 'proceed anyway' was considered and DECLINED.",

    "CLIMB RECEIPT (DEPLOY-UNHEALTHY-1, this change): the NEXT TRIGGER landed on the SERVICE-PROCESS facet and the rung it establishes is named honestly. CEILING 3 IS REACHED FOR THAT FACET: the service-process observation now types an unhealthy-but-observed process as its own arm (ProcessObservedUnhealthy, inside MemberObserved, distinct from MemberUnobservable) and the plan derives a replace-release step from it when the installed revision differs -- the ceiling as this row wrote it, no further. THE FACET IS NOT CLOSED: ceiling 3 is the ceiling this row stated, so the route now does everything the row claimed it could; what remains OUTSIDE the row is a different subject (a service unhealthy for a reason a replacement cannot fix, which the same arm now refuses loudly as UnhealthyAtInstalledRelease / UnhealthyReleasePositionUnobserved rather than deadlocking). THE DOOR-CUTOVER FACET IS UNCHANGED AND ITS REFUSAL IS NOT CLIMBED: CutoverJournalNotReadable refuses exactly as before (CONTROL-verified), and the cyclic precondition was removed by the ordering that already existed -- the gate runs downstream of the fold, which restarts the store -- not by relaxing the gate. CLAIMS AND THEIR STATE ON MAIN (test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_deploy_witness): plans_a_replacement_over_an_answered_503_at_a_different_revision, the_replacement_plan_carries_exactly_the_drift_and_nothing_invented, the_unhealthy_process_decision_is_replace and an_answered_503_is_never_refused_as_unobservable are the REDS -- RED on main because main has no ProcessObservedUnhealthy constructor at all, so the observation they supply does not exist there; the reply they stand for produced MemberUnobservable and refused the whole plan, which is this row's second and third occurrences. a_transport_failure_still_refuses and its no-status/no-response companions, a_body_naming_a_release_is_that_release_even_at_503 and the 403 guard are CONTROLS, green on both: the guards the row demanded are shown to survive the change. a_502_journal_read_still_refuses_the_cutover_with_no_route_effect, the_apply_gate_still_refuses_an_unreadable_journal_in_the_ledgers_words, the_journal_refusal_appends_to_a_refused_plan_and_stands_alone_otherwise and the two ordering witnesses are CONTROLS, green on both -- facet (b) changed nothing. The inhabitance claim is test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_probe_wet_witness (a real loopback listener answering 503 behind the real bounded GET yields HealthzAnsweredUnhealthy, and no listener still yields HealthzProbeRefused), a LocalRepoWetLane file per gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.member_identity", decl_name: "decide_member", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.member_identity", decl_name: "ProcessObservedUnhealthy", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.readiness", decl_name: "healthz_effective_read_from_status_get", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.live_deploy.tailnet_door_cutover", decl_name: "tailnet_door_cutover_run", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.live_deploy.observed_unhealthy_deploy_witness", decl_name: "plans_a_replacement_over_an_answered_503_at_a_different_revision", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
